  "//charts": "Reference tables for the chart sheet, laid out like the standard gojūon charts. LAYOUT ONLY where possible: a grid cell is a kana string (null = gap in the grid) and a flow item is a kana string, and app.js looks the romaji up from the decks below so the two can never disagree. A flow item may instead be {q, a} to carry its own reading — used for the extended katakana, which are reference-only and not in any deck. `type` is \"grid\" (consonant rows × vowel columns), \"flow\" (a wrapping list) or \"numbers\" (rows of {n, x, q, a} — what the row is, how it is written, the kana, the reading). `x` is optional and holds the kanji — 六, 二十, 百万, the form the drill puts on the square — while `n` names the row in plain terms, 6 or 20. A \"numbers\" section carries all four itself, because there is no deck of numbers to look a reading up from; every entry in the shipped one was generated by readNumber() and kanjiNumber() rather than typed, which is how the chart and the drills are kept from disagreeing. `wide` gives it one item per row, for a form too long to sit beside another.",
